v 3
d 'LILLARDHAZ': module to fit simultaneous-equations hazard/probit models with a Gaussian-copula correlation
d
d  lillardhaz fits two-equation simultaneous models in the style of
d  Lillard (1993): a probit or hazard equation 1 paired with a hazard
d  equation 2, linked through a single correlation parameter between
d  their underlying error terms, estimated jointly by maximum
d  likelihood via a Gaussian copula. Equation 1 may be a probit, a
d  log-normal hazard, or a piecewise (linear-log-hazard) Gompertz
d  hazard with an arbitrary number of user-specified nodes; equation 2
d  is always a hazard, log-normal or piecewise Gompertz. Fitting with
d  the nocorr option restricts the correlation to zero, which reduces
d  exactly to two independent univariate fits.
d
d  KW: survival analysis
d  KW: duration analysis
d  KW: simultaneous equations
d  KW: hazard model
d  KW: copula
d  KW: probit
d
d  Requires: Stata version 17
d
d  Distribution-Date: 20260925
d
d  Author: Nobutaka Fukuda, Tohoku University
d  Support: email nobutaka.fukuda@tohoku.ac.jp
d
